<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pōmārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		pomum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to fruit</i> or <i>fruit-trees</i>, <i>fruit-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seminarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 48</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pōmārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>a
			fruit-seller</i>, <i>fruiterer</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				3, 227</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 27</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 651,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pōmārĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A fruit-garden</i>, <i>orchard</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 2, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 5,
			10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Arb. 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen.
				15, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 122, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				7, 14</span></i>; Ov. de Nuce, 111; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Dan.
				13, 4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A store-room for fruit</i>, <i>a
				fruit-loft</i>, <i>fruitery</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R.
				R. 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 16, 18, § 59</span></i>
			(acc. to <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 23</span></i> P., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pōmārĭus</span></b> , ii,
				m., sc. locus, but without proof).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
